WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.583
<b>Here, Lord Krishna says to Arjuna:</b>

2
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:34.125
<b>"O mighty-armed one (Mahabaho),</b>

3
00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:39.000
<b>the person whose senses have completely </b>
<b>withdrawn from their objects</b>

4
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.333
<b>should be considered firmly</b>
<b>established in perfect wisdom."</b>

5
00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:51.500
<b>Krishna is making a definitive statement here</b>

6
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:59.083
<b>that complete detachment of all senses</b>
<b>from their objects is the path to steady wisdom.</b>

7
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:03.916
<b>The discussion here isn't about just </b>
<b>some senses or temporary restraint.</b>

8
00:01:03.916 --> 00:01:07.208
<b>Krishna uses a specific word here</b>

9
00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:08.208
<b>- 'Sarvashah'</b>

10
00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:10.541
<b>- meaning completely.</b>

11
00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:17.125
<b>It refers to the total withdrawal of </b>
<b>all senses from all objects in all situations.</b>

12
00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:22.041
<b>Here, Krishna also addresses Arjuna as</b>
<b>'Mahabaho'</b>

13
00:01:22.041 --> 00:01:26.708
<b>'Mahabaho' - one with mighty arms.</b>

14
00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.166
<b>It's as if He's saying,</b>

15
00:01:28.166 --> 00:01:34.000
<b>"Arjuna, just as the strength of your </b>
<b>arms has conquered enemies until now,</b>

16
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.250
<b>the time has come to </b>
<b>conquer your senses as well."</b>

17
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:48.250
<b>Perhaps this question arises in your mind:</b>

18
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:57.250
<b>Aren't our senses responsible for experiencing</b>
<b>touch, music, taste, and other pleasures? </b>

19
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:04.583
<b>If we completely detach our </b>
<b>senses from worldly objects,</b>

20
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:09.500
<b>won't life become dull and empty?</b>

21
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:16.500
<b>And am I wishing such a </b>
<b>bland existence for Arjuna?</b>

22
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.916
<b>No,</b>

23
00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:25.958
<b>I want both Arjuna and you </b>
<b>to make your life purposeful,</b>

24
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:31.375
<b>which never means living without joy.</b>

25
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:33.750
<b>Think back to a time</b>

26
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:38.875
<b>when you were pursuing a significant goal,</b>

27
00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:40.500
<b>and finally</b>

28
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.916
<b>achieved it.</b>

29
00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:49.291
<b>Remember that deep sense of fulfillment.</b>

30
00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:56.541
<b>Now recall how you maintained</b>
<b>focus to reach that goal,</b>

31
00:02:56.541 --> 00:03:02.333
<b>how you prevented your mind from wandering,</b>

32
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:03.500
<b>perhaps</b>

33
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:09.708
<b>even temporarily gave up </b>
<b>some forms of entertainment</b>

34
00:03:09.708 --> 00:03:11.083
<b>– but</b>

35
00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:14.875
<b>did that make life joyless?</b>

36
00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:20.291
<b>On the contrary, that focus and self-control</b>

37
00:03:20.291 --> 00:03:26.583
<b>led you to experience the </b>
<b>profound joy of achievement.</b>

38
00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:28.291
<b>Control</b>

39
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.791
<b>is not joylessness.</b>

40
00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:40.166
<b>A purposeful life is not a dull life,</b>
<b>but rather one filled with bliss.</b>

41
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:44.625
<b>Another doubt may arise</b>

42
00:03:44.625 --> 00:03:49.708
<b>– that temporary control is understandable,</b>

43
00:03:49.708 --> 00:03:50.916
<b>but</b>

44
00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:53.083
<b>complete control?</b>

45
00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:55.958
<b>Such a demanding request?</b>

46
00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:58.958
<b>The greater the goal,</b>

47
00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:03.833
<b>the greater the control needed.</b>

48
00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:06.041
<b>If the goal is small,</b>

49
00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:10.791
<b>like a weekly class test,</b>

50
00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:14.375
<b>then minimal control suffices.</b>

51
00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:15.750
<b>But</b>

52
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:20.750
<b>if you're preparing for annual examinations,</b>

53
00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.708
<b>greater control becomes necessary.</b>

54
00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:28.083
<b>And consider this</b>

55
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:32.166
<b>– here we're discussing life transformation,</b>

56
00:04:32.166 --> 00:04:38.833
<b>a goal where every moment will be filled with joy.</b>

57
00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:45.750
<b>For such supreme happiness, </b>
<b>complete control becomes essential.</b>

58
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.083
<b>I know this</b>

59
00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:51.875
<b>sounds challenging to hear.</b>

60
00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:52.958
<b>But</b>

61
00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.750
<b>it's simply a matter of practice.</b>

62
00:04:55.750 --> 00:05:00.000
<b>After practice, everything becomes easier,</b>

63
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.333
<b>and humans begin to find joy in it.</b>

64
00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:08.166
<b>Remember –</b>

65
00:05:08.166 --> 00:05:12.375
<b>when someone first learns to drive a vehicle,</b>

66
00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:20.000
<b>controlling it is difficult, there's fear of accidents</b>

67
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.250
<b>– but today,</b>

68
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.958
<b>after practicing complete control,</b>

69
00:05:23.958 --> 00:05:27.416
<b>that same vehicle becomes a source of joy,</b>

70
00:05:27.416 --> 00:05:32.333
<b>a means of utility.</b>

71
00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:38.000
<b>Controlling life's vehicle is a path to supreme joy;</b>

72
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.583
<b>it just needs some practice.</b>

73
00:05:42.583 --> 00:05:44.125
<b>Keep at it.</b>

74
00:05:48.791 --> 00:05:54.166
<b>In today's society, everyone </b>
<b>is caught up in attachments.</b>

75
00:05:54.166 --> 00:05:55.875
<b>Attachment to power.</b>

76
00:05:55.875 --> 00:05:57.958
<b>Attachment to beauty.</b>

77
00:05:57.958 --> 00:06:00.625
<b>Attachment to wealth.</b>

78
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:03.583
<b>And why?</b>

79
00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:08.291
<b>So that one can influence others.</b>

80
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:13.791
<b>Power and authority are desired to control others.</b>

81
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:18.666
<b>Beauty is desired to gain others' admiration.</b>

82
00:06:18.666 --> 00:06:25.625
<b>Wealth is accumulated to</b>
<b>have better amenities than others.</b>

83
00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:29.250
<b>Think again –</b>

84
00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:36.041
<b>is such an attached person truly powerful?</b>

85
00:06:36.041 --> 00:06:37.541
<b>No.</b>

86
00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:40.083
<b>They are powerless,</b>

87
00:06:40.083 --> 00:06:46.625
<b>for they have handed over </b>
<b>their existence's reins to others.</b>

88
00:06:46.625 --> 00:06:51.166
<b>Their happiness lies in others' control.</b>

89
00:06:51.166 --> 00:06:56.166
<b>If someone disobeys, the illusion of power breaks;</b>

90
00:06:56.166 --> 00:07:00.791
<b>if praise isn't received,</b>
<b>the illusion of beauty shatters;</b>

91
00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:05.083
<b>if someone else has better amenities,</b>

92
00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:07.875
<b>the illusion of wealth crumbles.</b>

93
00:07:07.875 --> 00:07:11.916
<b>This is endless...</b>

94
00:07:11.916 --> 00:07:19.666
<b>How unfortunate it is to make one's life </b>
<b>dependent on others' reactions.</b>

95
00:07:19.666 --> 00:07:25.416
<b>Running after such attachments </b>
<b>is merely weakness.</b>

96
00:07:25.416 --> 00:07:26.833
<b>So then,</b>

97
00:07:26.833 --> 00:07:30.375
<b>what is true power?</b>

98
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:38.666
<b>Living according to right values, </b>
<b>not according to others' praise and reactions.</b>

99
00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:40.958
<b>Being able to control the mind,</b>

100
00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:47.583
<b>making decisions based </b>
<b>on your goals in any situation,</b>

101
00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:51.166
<b>rather than being compelled by sensory desires.</b>

102
00:07:51.166 --> 00:07:53.708
<b>When this happens,</b>

103
00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:58.000
<b>life's happiness won't depend on others.</b>

104
00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.791
<b>This is complete independence.</b>

105
00:08:02.791 --> 00:08:04.583
<b>Know this truth,</b>

106
00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.500
<b>embrace it yourself,</b>

107
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.500
<b>and</b>

108
00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.416
<b>inspire your family too.</b>

109
00:08:15.083 --> 00:08:17.458
<b>Success/failure,</b>

110
00:08:17.458 --> 00:08:22.750
<b>ups/downs are all part of professional life.</b>

111
00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:29.208
<b>Whether you work independently</b>
<b>or hold a leadership position.</b>

112
00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:34.416
<b>In both situations, professional growth requires</b>

113
00:08:34.416 --> 00:08:37.958
<b>that you remain unshaken in crisis</b>

114
00:08:37.958 --> 00:08:38.875
<b>and</b>

115
00:08:38.875 --> 00:08:44.375
<b>make clear decisions in any circumstance.</b>

116
00:08:44.375 --> 00:08:48.125
<b>This requires mental stability,</b>

117
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:49.541
<b>ontrol over yourself </b>

118
00:08:49.541 --> 00:08:56.208
<b>– that is, control over your senses.</b>

119
00:08:56.208 --> 00:09:00.750
<b>You must have seen or heard instances</b>

120
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:08.083
<b>where someone, in the greed for profit, </b>
<b>committed something unethical or criminal,</b>

121
00:09:08.083 --> 00:09:09.416
<b>got caught,</b>

122
00:09:09.416 --> 00:09:13.291
<b>and their reputation was destroyed.</b>

123
00:09:13.291 --> 00:09:20.541
<b>Someone lost control, said or </b>
<b>did something wrong to a colleague </b>

124
00:09:20.541 --> 00:09:23.041
<b>– paid a heavy price.</b>

125
00:09:23.041 --> 00:09:28.541
<b>Someone, becoming unstable, made </b>
<b>wrong business decisions in difficult times,</b>

126
00:09:28.541 --> 00:09:32.375
<b>making the situation worse.</b>

127
00:09:32.375 --> 00:09:37.500
<b>Even a small crack can bring</b>
<b>down an entire building.</b>

128
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:41.208
<b>It cannot be ignored.</b>

129
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:48.625
<b>Often, one wrong decision, a moment's loss </b>
<b>of control, can prove costly.</b>

130
00:09:48.625 --> 00:09:51.083
<b>Stay vigilant.</b>

131
00:09:51.083 --> 00:09:55.250
<b>But this isn't cause for fear either.</b>

132
00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.083
<b>Just keep progressing spiritually,</b>

133
00:09:59.083 --> 00:10:01.750
<b>speak/listen to good things,</b>

134
00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.875
<b>keep practicing control.</b>

135
00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:11.041
<b>This will purify the mind, keep intelligence stable,</b>

136
00:10:11.041 --> 00:10:13.333
<b>maintain control,</b>

137
00:10:13.333 --> 00:10:16.791
<b>and prevent wrong decisions.</b>

